window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/security-v27-085-8a78d8a1e8e9082d.json"]={sha256:"8a78d8a1e8e9082d30b04c45aa353bbc8015346687500da5d856767cf351fb39",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v27-case-4beae8d416dc5832","url":"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/warm-standby.html","title":"PostgreSQL 18 log-shipping standby servers","titleEn":"PostgreSQL 18 log-shipping standby servers","publisher":"PostgreSQL","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-085","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"security-v27-085","related":[{"id":"security-v27-086","referenceUrls":["https://restic.readthedocs.io/en/stable/060_forget.html"],"title":"restic：快照可達集合、共享區塊與清理的安全邊界","titleEn":"restic: snapshot reachability, shared chunks and cleanup boundaries","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付wal-balance.csv、capacity-horizon.json、slot-assumptions.md與recovery-tradeoffs.md，標明數值是教學假設而非產品預設。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver wal-balance.csv, capacity-horizon.json, slot-assumptions.md and recovery-tradeoffs.md. Label the quantities as teaching assumptions rather than defaults, and preserve separate capacity and recoverability conclusions.","difference":"建立快照到內容區塊的引用圖，計算保留快照可達聯集及不可達區塊；只輸出模擬清理計畫，不執行真實forget或prune。","differenceEn":"Build a snapshot-to-content reference graph and calculate the union reachable from retained snapshots plus unreachable chunks. Produce only a simulated cleanup plan, without running real forget or prune commands.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["PostgreSQL replication slot可避免必要WAL被過早回收，也可能保留到填滿磁碟；設定保留上限會改變失聯備援是否仍能追上，不是免費保證。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 已扣除其他使用後可給新增WAL的空間120GB，產生速率6GB/小時，備援消耗0；所有GB採十進位且速率固定。 淨增加6GB/小時，120/6=20小時耗盡；若消耗恢復2GB/小時，淨增加4，耗盡時間延為30小時。","restic區分移除快照參照與清理不再需要的資料；本課以每區塊1MB且無封裝額外成本建模，實際釋放空間還受pack與重打包影響。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 S1引用a,b,c,d；S2引用c,d,e；S3引用d,e,f。全庫6個區塊，保留S2與S3，移除S1的引用。 保留聯集c,d,e,f共4MB，不可達a,b共2MB；S1的4MB不能全部清理，因c,d仍共享。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["PostgreSQL replication slots can prevent needed WAL from being recycled, but retention can fill storage. A retention cap changes whether a disconnected standby can catch up; it is not a cost-free guarantee. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. After accounting for other use, 120 decimal GB remain available for additional WAL. Generation is six GB per hour and consumption zero; rates are fixed for this teaching scenario. Net retention grows by six GB per hour, exhausting 120 GB in twenty hours. Restoring consumption to two GB per hour reduces net growth to four and extends exhaustion time to thirty hours.","restic separates removing snapshot references from pruning unneeded data. The model gives each chunk one MB with no packaging overhead; actual reclaimed space also depends on packs and repacking behavior. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. S1 references a,b,c,d; S2 references c,d,e; S3 references d,e,f. The repository has six chunks. Retain S2 and S3 while removing only the S1 snapshot reference. The retained union c,d,e,f totals four MB; unreachable a,b total two MB. S1 four-MB content cannot all be reclaimed because c and d remain shared by retained snapshots.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"security-v27-095","referenceUrls":["https://sre.google/sre-book/being-on-call/"],"title":"Google SRE值班：事件後續工作與可持續負荷帳本","titleEn":"Google SRE on-call: follow-up work and sustainable load accounting","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付wal-balance.csv、capacity-horizon.json、slot-assumptions.md與recovery-tradeoffs.md，標明數值是教學假設而非產品預設。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver wal-balance.csv, capacity-horizon.json, slot-assumptions.md and recovery-tradeoffs.md. Label the quantities as teaching assumptions rather than defaults, and preserve separate capacity and recoverability conclusions.","difference":"將合成事件分為即時處理與後續工作，逐件保存工時及負責人；比較自動化前後總負荷，不能把縮短接警時間等同消除事件成本。","differenceEn":"Separate immediate incident response from follow-up work and record hours and owner per synthetic event. Compare total workload before and after automation without equating faster acknowledgment with eliminated incident cost.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["PostgreSQL replication slot可避免必要WAL被過早回收，也可能保留到填滿磁碟；設定保留上限會改變失聯備援是否仍能追上，不是免費保證。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 已扣除其他使用後可給新增WAL的空間120GB，產生速率6GB/小時，備援消耗0；所有GB採十進位且速率固定。 淨增加6GB/小時，120/6=20小時耗盡；若消耗恢復2GB/小時，淨增加4，耗盡時間延為30小時。","SRE值班實務重視可持續工作量與工程改善；本課40小時分母及工作時間均為教學假設，並非所有組織的工時標準或人力建議。 本課所有數值、事件與系統狀態均為原創合成資料；只在本機檔案與授權隔離練習中處理，不接觸生產設備或他人資料。 一個合成週可用工程時間40小時；10件事件各即時處理1小時、後續1.5小時，無重疊工時計入，其他工作暫排除。 完整事件工時10×(1+1.5)=25小時，占62.5%；只計即時處理會報10小時、25%，漏掉15小時。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["PostgreSQL replication slots can prevent needed WAL from being recycled, but retention can fill storage. A retention cap changes whether a disconnected standby can catch up; it is not a cost-free guarantee. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. After accounting for other use, 120 decimal GB remain available for additional WAL. Generation is six GB per hour and consumption zero; rates are fixed for this teaching scenario. Net retention grows by six GB per hour, exhausting 120 GB in twenty hours. Restoring consumption to two GB per hour reduces net growth to four and extends exhaustion time to thirty hours.","SRE on-call practice emphasizes sustainable workload and engineering improvement. The forty-hour denominator and task durations are teaching assumptions, not a universal workweek standard or staffing recommendation. Every quantity, event and system state below is original synthetic teaching data. Work only on local files or an explicitly authorized isolated lab, without production access or other people’s data. A synthetic week provides forty engineering hours. Ten incidents each require one immediate-response hour and 1.5 follow-up hours, counted without overlapping person-hours; other work is excluded from this fixture. Total incident work is 10×(1+1.5)=25 hours, or 62.5%. Counting only response would report ten hours and 25%, omitting fifteen hours of required follow-up.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v27-case-fefc3bf02d30922f","url":"https://restic.readthedocs.io/en/stable/060_forget.html","title":"restic removing snapshots and pruning","titleEn":"restic removing snapshots and pruning","publisher":"restic","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-121ad2356e8597a4","url":"https://sre.google/sre-book/being-on-call/","title":"Google SRE Book: being on-call","titleEn":"Google SRE Book: being on-call","publisher":"Google","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
